(The reader is standing on the '%' at position. Consumes the flags, the
 width, and the one letter that follows - or, if what follows is not a
 sequence this library knows, consumes nothing but the '%' itself, which
 GNU also just copies through. Answers where to continue from.)
To 'write one escape at' with a buffer called format and a number called length and a number called position and a number called moment and a buffer called output.
  a number called i is position add 1.
  a number called 'pad flag' is 0.
  a number called 'case flag' is 0.
  a number called c is 0.
  a boolean called 'still a flag' is true.
  While 'still a flag' and i is less than or equal to length,
    set c to byte i of format,
    set 'still a flag' to false,
    if c is '-' then, set 'pad flag' to '-', set 'still a flag' to true.
    if c is '_' then, set 'pad flag' to '_', set 'still a flag' to true.
    if c is '0' then, set 'pad flag' to '0', set 'still a flag' to true.
    if c is '^' then, set 'case flag' to '^', set 'still a flag' to true.
    if c is '#' then, set 'case flag' to '#', set 'still a flag' to true.
    if 'still a flag' then, increment i..
  Create a buffer called digits.
  a boolean called 'still a digit' is true.
  While 'still a digit' and i is less than or equal to length,
    set c to byte i of format,
    set 'still a digit' to false,
    if c is greater than or equal to '0' and c is less than or equal to '9' then, set 'still a digit' to true.
    if 'still a digit' then, 'write the byte' with c and digits, increment i..
  a number called width is -1.
  If digits's size is greater than 0 then, a text called 'the width text' is "{digits}", set width to 'the width text' as a number.
  If i is greater than length then, 'write the byte' with '%' and output, Return a number, i.
  set c to byte i of format.
  a boolean called 'it was written' is 'write a specifier' with output and moment and c and 'pad flag' and 'case flag' and width.
  If 'it was written' is false then, 'write the byte' with '%' and output, Return a number, position add 1.
  Return a number, i add 1.

(The one export: any layout, walked byte by byte, with a '%'-sequence
 handed to 'write one escape at' and everything else copied straight
 through.)
To 'the moment written as' of a number called moment and a text called layout.
  Create a buffer called output.
  a buffer called format is "{layout}".
  a number called 'the length' is format's size.
  a number called position is 1.
  a number called 'the byte' is 0.
  While position is less than or equal to 'the length',
    set 'the byte' to byte position of format,
    if 'the byte' is '%' then, set position to {'write one escape at' with format and 'the length' and position and moment and output}.
    if 'the byte' is not '%' then, 'write the byte' with 'the byte' and output, increment position..
  Return a text, "{output}".

To 'the date of' of a number called moment.
  Return a text, {'the moment written as' of moment and "%F"}.

To 'the date and time of' of a number called moment.
  Return a text, {'the moment written as' of moment and "%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S+00:00"}.

To 'the rfc 3339 date and time of' of a number called moment.
  Return a text, {'the moment written as' of moment and "%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%S+00:00"}.

To 'the rfc email date of' of a number called moment.
  Return a text, {'the moment written as' of moment and "%a, %d %b %Y %T %z"}.

To 'the moment in words of' of a number called moment.
  Return a text, {'the moment written as' of moment and "%a %b %e %H:%M:%S %Z %Y"}.

(--- Reading a moment in. A reader is a map holding "position", the byte
 it is standing on, counting from 1 - the same shape json's reader uses,
 minus a "failed" flag, because every step here either advances the
 reader on success or puts it back exactly where it found it on failure,
 so a caller can always try the next form clean. )

To 'the byte at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader.
  a number called position is reader's "position".
  If position is less than 1 then, Return a number, 0.
  If position is greater than document's size then, Return a number, 0.
  Return a number, byte position of document.

To 'step past the byte' with a map called reader.
  a number called position is reader's "position".
  Set reader's "position" to position add 1.

(Skips ' ' only - the one separator every accepted form uses - and
 answers how many were skipped, so a caller can tell "at least one" from
 "none at all".)
To 'skip spaces' with a buffer called document and a map called reader.
  a number called 'how many' is 0.
  a number called 'the byte' is 'the byte at' with document and reader.
  While 'the byte' is ' ',
    'step past the byte' with reader,
    increment 'how many',
    set 'the byte' to 'the byte at' with document and reader.
  Return a number, 'how many'.

(Does the document read word, case-sensitively, where the reader is
 standing? Steps past it on a match; leaves the reader untouched on a
 miss, so a caller can try something else.)
To 'the document reads' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a text called word.
  a buffer called wanted is "{word}".
  a number called 'letters wanted' is wanted's size.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a number called position is start.
  a number called 'letters matched' is 0.
  a boolean called 'still matching' is true.
  While 'still matching' and 'letters matched' is less than 'letters wanted',
    a number called 'the byte found' is 'the byte at' with document and reader,
    a number called 'the byte wanted' is byte {'letters matched' add 1} of wanted,
    set 'still matching' to false,
    if 'the byte found' is 'the byte wanted' then, set 'still matching' to true.
    if 'still matching' then, 'step past the byte' with reader, increment 'letters matched'..
  If 'still matching' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Return a boolean, false.
  Return a boolean, true.

(One ASCII letter, folded to lower case: everything but 'A'..'Z' passes
 through unchanged, which is exactly right for a digit, a space, or a
 punctuation byte.)
To 'folded to lower case' of a number called 'the byte'.
  If 'the byte' is greater than or equal to 'A' and 'the byte' is less than or equal to 'Z' then, Return a number, 'the byte' add 32.
  Return a number, 'the byte'.

(The case-insensitive twin of 'the document reads': word is given in
 lower case, and every letter the document offers is folded to lower case
 before it is compared.)
To 'the document reads ignoring case' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a text called word.
  a buffer called wanted is "{word}".
  a number called 'letters wanted' is wanted's size.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a number called 'letters matched' is 0.
  a boolean called 'still matching' is true.
  While 'still matching' and 'letters matched' is less than 'letters wanted',
    a number called 'the byte found' is 'folded to lower case' of {'the byte at' with document and reader},
    a number called 'the byte wanted' is byte {'letters matched' add 1} of wanted,
    set 'still matching' to false,
    if 'the byte found' is 'the byte wanted' then, set 'still matching' to true.
    if 'still matching' then, 'step past the byte' with reader, increment 'letters matched'..
  If 'still matching' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Return a boolean, false.
  Return a boolean, true.

(Exactly count digits, fixed width - the shape every field of the
 compact and dashed forms takes. Answers the value, or -1 with the
 reader put back where it started, when fewer than count digits are
 there to read.)
To 'read exactly' with a number called count and a buffer called document and a map called reader.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  Create a buffer called digits.
  a number called i is 0.
  a boolean called ok is true.
  While ok and i is less than count,
    a number called b is 'the byte at' with document and reader,
    set ok to false,
    if b is greater than or equal to '0' and b is less than or equal to '9' then, set ok to true.
    if ok then, 'write the byte' with b and digits, 'step past the byte' with reader, increment i..
  If i is less than count then, Set reader's "position" to start, Return a number, -1.
  a text called figures is "{digits}".
  Return a number, figures as a number.

(One or more digits, however many there are - the shape a human-typed
 year, day, or clock component takes. Written into the outcome map's
 "matched" and "value"; the reader does not move at all when there is no
 digit to read.)
To 'read some digits into' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called outcome.
  Create a buffer called digits.
  a number called b is 'the byte at' with document and reader.
  a boolean called 'still a digit' is false.
  If b is greater than or equal to '0' and b is less than or equal to '9' then, set 'still a digit' to true.
  While 'still a digit',
    'write the byte' with b and digits,
    'step past the byte' with reader,
    set b to 'the byte at' with document and reader,
    set 'still a digit' to false,
    if b is greater than or equal to '0' and b is less than or equal to '9' then, set 'still a digit' to true..
  If digits's size is 0 then, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Set outcome's "value" to 0, Return.
  a text called figures is "{digits}".
  Set outcome's "matched" to true.
  Set outcome's "value" to {figures as a number}.

(A space, tab, newline, or carriage return - the same four bytes json's
 'is whitespace' names.)
To 'is a space byte' of a number called 'the byte'.
  Return a boolean, 'the byte' is ' ' or 'the byte' is '\t' or 'the byte' is '\n' or 'the byte' is '\r'.

(Leading and trailing space, tab, newline, and carriage return removed -
 every accepted form is read "after trimming".)
To 'the trimmed text of' of a text called words.
  a buffer called letters is "{words}".
  a number called 'the length' is letters's size.
  a number called start is 1.
  a number called 'the end' is 'the length'.
  a number called b is 0.
  a boolean called 'still whitespace at the start' is true.
  While start is less than or equal to 'the end' and 'still whitespace at the start',
    set b to byte start of letters,
    set 'still whitespace at the start' to 'is a space byte' of b,
    if 'still whitespace at the start' then, increment start..
  a boolean called 'still whitespace at the end' is true.
  While 'the end' is greater than or equal to start and 'still whitespace at the end',
    set b to byte 'the end' of letters,
    set 'still whitespace at the end' to 'is a space byte' of b,
    if 'still whitespace at the end' then, decrement 'the end'..
  Create a buffer called trimmed.
  For each position from start to 'the end', 'write the byte' with {byte position of letters} and trimmed.
  Return a text, "{trimmed}".

(An optional UTC offset: Z, or a signed hh:mm, hhmm, or bare hh, applied
 by SUBTRACTING it from a local reading to land on UTC. Written into the
 outcome map's "matched" and "seconds"; not present is not a failure, so
 the reader is left untouched and "matched" is simply false.)
To 'read an offset into' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called outcome.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a boolean called 'it reads z' is 'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "z".
  If 'it reads z' then, Set outcome's "matched" to true, Set outcome's "seconds" to 0, Return.
  a number called c is 'the byte at' with document and reader.
  a number called 'the sign' is 0.
  If c is '+' then, set 'the sign' to 1.
  If c is '-' then, set 'the sign' to -1.
  If 'the sign' is 0 then, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Set outcome's "seconds" to 0, Return.
  'step past the byte' with reader.
  a number called 'the hour' is 'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader.
  If 'the hour' is less than 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Set outcome's "seconds" to 0, Return.
  a number called 'the minute' is 0.
  a boolean called 'it has a colon' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and ":".
  If 'it has a colon' then, set 'the minute' to {'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader}.
  If 'it has a colon' and 'the minute' is less than 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Set outcome's "seconds" to 0, Return.
  If 'it has a colon' is false then, a number called 'the fused minute' is 'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader, if 'the fused minute' is greater than or equal to 0 then, set 'the minute' to 'the fused minute'..
  a number called 'the offset seconds' is {'the hour' multiply 3600} add {'the minute' multiply 60}.
  Set outcome's "matched" to true.
  Set outcome's "seconds" to {'the sign' multiply 'the offset seconds'}.

(A month's full or short English name, case-insensitively - the full
 names tried first, since a short name is a prefix of its own full one
 and would otherwise steal the match. 0 when neither is there.)
To 'read a month name at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "january"} then, Return a number, 1.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "february"} then, Return a number, 2.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "march"} then, Return a number, 3.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "april"} then, Return a number, 4.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "may"} then, Return a number, 5.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "june"} then, Return a number, 6.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "july"} then, Return a number, 7.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "august"} then, Return a number, 8.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "september"} then, Return a number, 9.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "october"} then, Return a number, 10.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "november"} then, Return a number, 11.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "december"} then, Return a number, 12.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "jan"} then, Return a number, 1.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "feb"} then, Return a number, 2.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "mar"} then, Return a number, 3.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "apr"} then, Return a number, 4.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "jun"} then, Return a number, 6.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "jul"} then, Return a number, 7.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "aug"} then, Return a number, 8.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "sep"} then, Return a number, 9.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "oct"} then, Return a number, 10.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "nov"} then, Return a number, 11.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "dec"} then, Return a number, 12.
  Return a number, 0.

(A weekday's full or short English name, case-insensitively, full names
 first for the same reason. 0 when neither is there.)
To 'read a weekday name at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "monday"} then, Return a number, 1.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "tuesday"} then, Return a number, 2.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "wednesday"} then, Return a number, 3.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "thursday"} then, Return a number, 4.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "friday"} then, Return a number, 5.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "saturday"} then, Return a number, 6.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "sunday"} then, Return a number, 7.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "mon"} then, Return a number, 1.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "tue"} then, Return a number, 2.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "wed"} then, Return a number, 3.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "thu"} then, Return a number, 4.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "fri"} then, Return a number, 5.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "sat"} then, Return a number, 6.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "sun"} then, Return a number, 7.
  Return a number, 0.

(H:M, or H:M:S - each component any number of digits, as a person types
 one. Written into the outcome map's "matched", "hour", "minute", and
 "second"; the reader is put back where it found this if the shape is
 not there after all.)
To 'try a clock time at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called outcome.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a map called scratch is {"matched": false, "value": 0}.
  'read some digits into' with document and reader and scratch.
  a boolean called 'the hour matched' is scratch's "matched".
  If 'the hour matched' is false then, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the hour' is scratch's "value".
  a boolean called 'has the first colon' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and ":".
  If 'has the first colon' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  Set scratch's "matched" to false.
  'read some digits into' with document and reader and scratch.
  a boolean called 'the minute matched' is scratch's "matched".
  If 'the minute matched' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the minute' is scratch's "value".
  a number called 'the second' is 0.
  a boolean called 'has the second colon' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and ":".
  If 'has the second colon' then, Set scratch's "matched" to false, 'read some digits into' with document and reader and scratch, if scratch's "matched" is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return..
  If 'has the second colon' then, set 'the second' to {scratch's "value"}.
  Set outcome's "matched" to true.
  Set outcome's "hour" to 'the hour'.
  Set outcome's "minute" to 'the minute'.
  Set outcome's "second" to 'the second'.

(Each of the five absolute forms below is a try: it either matches and
 leaves the reader just past what it consumed, or it does not and puts
 the reader back exactly where it found it, writing only outcome's
 "matched" (and, on a match, "moment"). None of them raises the error
 flag - that is what makes trying the next one, on a miss, safe.)

To 'try the epoch form at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called outcome.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a boolean called 'has the at sign' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and "@".
  If 'has the at sign' is false then, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the sign' is 1.
  a boolean called 'it is negative' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and "-".
  If 'it is negative' then, set 'the sign' to -1.
  a map called scratch is {"matched": false, "value": 0}.
  'read some digits into' with document and reader and scratch.
  a boolean called 'digits matched' is scratch's "matched".
  If 'digits matched' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the value' is scratch's "value".
  Set outcome's "matched" to true.
  Set outcome's "moment" to {'the sign' multiply 'the value'}.

(YYYYMMDD, optionally 'T'HHMMSS - fixed width throughout, and no offset:
 the plan gives this form none.)
To 'try the compact form at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called outcome.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a number called 'the year' is 'read exactly' with 4 and document and reader.
  If 'the year' is less than 0 then, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the month' is 'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader.
  If 'the month' is less than 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the day of month' is 'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader.
  If 'the day of month' is less than 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the hour' is 0.
  a number called 'the minute' is 0.
  a number called 'the second' is 0.
  a boolean called 'has a time part' is 'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "t".
  If 'has a time part' then, set 'the hour' to {'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader}.
  If 'has a time part' and 'the hour' is less than 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  If 'has a time part' then, set 'the minute' to {'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader}.
  If 'has a time part' and 'the minute' is less than 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  If 'has a time part' then, set 'the second' to {'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader}.
  If 'has a time part' and 'the second' is less than 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the next byte' is 'the byte at' with document and reader.
  a boolean called 'the next byte is a digit' is false.
  If 'the next byte' is greater than or equal to '0' and 'the next byte' is less than or equal to '9' then, set 'the next byte is a digit' to true.
  If 'the next byte is a digit' then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a boolean called 'the date is valid' is 'is a valid date' of 'the year' and 'the month' and 'the day of month'.
  If 'the date is valid' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a boolean called 'the time is valid' is 'is a valid time' of 'the hour' and 'the minute' and 'the second'.
  If 'the time is valid' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  Set outcome's "matched" to true.
  Set outcome's "moment" to {'the moment at' with 'the year' and 'the month' and 'the day of month' and 'the hour' and 'the minute' and 'the second'}.

(YYYY-MM-DD, optionally (' '|'T')HH:MM:SS, optionally an offset - the
 only one of the five with an offset, per the plan.)
To 'try the dashed iso form at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called outcome.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a number called 'the year' is 'read exactly' with 4 and document and reader.
  If 'the year' is less than 0 then, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a boolean called 'has the first dash' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and "-".
  If 'has the first dash' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the month' is 'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader.
  If 'the month' is less than 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a boolean called 'has the second dash' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and "-".
  If 'has the second dash' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the day of month' is 'read exactly' with 2 and document and reader.
  If 'the day of month' is less than 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the hour' is 0.
  a number called 'the minute' is 0.
  a number called 'the second' is 0.
  a number called 'the position before the time part' is reader's "position".
  a boolean called 'has a separator' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and " ".
  If 'has a separator' is false then, set 'has a separator' to {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "t"}.
  a map called clock is {"matched": false, "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0}.
  If 'has a separator' then, 'try a clock time at' with document and reader and clock.
  a boolean called 'the time matched' is clock's "matched".
  If 'has a separator' and 'the time matched' then, set 'the hour' to {clock's "hour"}, set 'the minute' to {clock's "minute"}, set 'the second' to {clock's "second"}.
  If 'the time matched' is false then, Set reader's "position" to 'the position before the time part'.
  a boolean called 'the date is valid' is 'is a valid date' of 'the year' and 'the month' and 'the day of month'.
  If 'the date is valid' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a boolean called 'the time is valid' is 'is a valid time' of 'the hour' and 'the minute' and 'the second'.
  If 'the time is valid' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a map called offset is {"matched": false, "seconds": 0}.
  'read an offset into' with document and reader and offset.
  a number called 'the offset seconds' is 0.
  If offset's "matched" then, set 'the offset seconds' to {offset's "seconds"}.
  a number called 'the local moment' is {'the moment at' with 'the year' and 'the month' and 'the day of month' and 'the hour' and 'the minute' and 'the second'}.
  Set outcome's "matched" to true.
  Set outcome's "moment" to {'the local moment' subtract 'the offset seconds'}.

(DIGITS SPACE MONTHNAME SPACE DIGITS, optionally SPACE-then-clock-time -
 "29 Jul 2026" and "29 July 2026". A trailing time that does not parse is
 not this form's failure: the reader just lands after the year, midnight
 assumed, the way GNU reads a bare date with garbage after it.)
To 'try a day month year at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called outcome.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a map called scratch is {"matched": false, "value": 0}.
  'read some digits into' with document and reader and scratch.
  a boolean called 'day matched' is scratch's "matched".
  If 'day matched' is false then, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the day of month' is scratch's "value".
  a number called 'the spaces after the day' is 'skip spaces' with document and reader.
  If 'the spaces after the day' is 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the month' is 'read a month name at' with document and reader.
  If 'the month' is 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the spaces after the month' is 'skip spaces' with document and reader.
  If 'the spaces after the month' is 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  Set scratch's "matched" to false.
  'read some digits into' with document and reader and scratch.
  a boolean called 'year matched' is scratch's "matched".
  If 'year matched' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the year' is scratch's "value".
  a number called 'the position after the year' is reader's "position".
  a number called 'the spaces before the time' is 'skip spaces' with document and reader.
  a map called clock is {"matched": false, "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0}.
  'try a clock time at' with document and reader and clock.
  a number called 'the hour' is 0.
  a number called 'the minute' is 0.
  a number called 'the second' is 0.
  a boolean called 'the time matched' is clock's "matched".
  If 'the time matched' then, set 'the hour' to {clock's "hour"}, set 'the minute' to {clock's "minute"}, set 'the second' to {clock's "second"}.
  If 'the time matched' is false then, Set reader's "position" to 'the position after the year'.
  a boolean called 'the date is valid' is 'is a valid date' of 'the year' and 'the month' and 'the day of month'.
  If 'the date is valid' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a boolean called 'the time is valid' is 'is a valid time' of 'the hour' and 'the minute' and 'the second'.
  If 'the time is valid' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  Set outcome's "matched" to true.
  Set outcome's "moment" to {'the moment at' with 'the year' and 'the month' and 'the day of month' and 'the hour' and 'the minute' and 'the second'}.

(MONTHNAME SPACE DIGITS [','] SPACE DIGITS, optionally the same trailing
 time - "Jul 29 2026" and "July 29, 2026". The comma is optional either
 way; nothing here requires it.)
To 'try a month day year at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called outcome.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a number called 'the month' is 'read a month name at' with document and reader.
  If 'the month' is 0 then, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the spaces after the month' is 'skip spaces' with document and reader.
  If 'the spaces after the month' is 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a map called scratch is {"matched": false, "value": 0}.
  'read some digits into' with document and reader and scratch.
  a boolean called 'day matched' is scratch's "matched".
  If 'day matched' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the day of month' is scratch's "value".
  a boolean called 'had a comma' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and ",".
  a number called 'the spaces after the day' is 'skip spaces' with document and reader.
  If 'the spaces after the day' is 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  Set scratch's "matched" to false.
  'read some digits into' with document and reader and scratch.
  a boolean called 'year matched' is scratch's "matched".
  If 'year matched' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the year' is scratch's "value".
  a number called 'the position after the year' is reader's "position".
  a number called 'the spaces before the time' is 'skip spaces' with document and reader.
  a map called clock is {"matched": false, "hour": 0, "minute": 0, "second": 0}.
  'try a clock time at' with document and reader and clock.
  a number called 'the hour' is 0.
  a number called 'the minute' is 0.
  a number called 'the second' is 0.
  a boolean called 'the time matched' is clock's "matched".
  If 'the time matched' then, set 'the hour' to {clock's "hour"}, set 'the minute' to {clock's "minute"}, set 'the second' to {clock's "second"}.
  If 'the time matched' is false then, Set reader's "position" to 'the position after the year'.
  a boolean called 'the date is valid' is 'is a valid date' of 'the year' and 'the month' and 'the day of month'.
  If 'the date is valid' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a boolean called 'the time is valid' is 'is a valid time' of 'the hour' and 'the minute' and 'the second'.
  If 'the time is valid' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  Set outcome's "matched" to true.
  Set outcome's "moment" to {'the moment at' with 'the year' and 'the month' and 'the day of month' and 'the hour' and 'the minute' and 'the second'}.

(Every accepted absolute form, tried in turn; the first one to match
 wins. Written into outcome's "matched" and "moment", exactly as each of
 the five it calls does.)
To 'try an absolute moment at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called outcome.
  'try the epoch form at' with document and reader and outcome.
  a boolean called 'matched the epoch form' is outcome's "matched".
  If 'matched the epoch form' then, Return.
  'try the dashed iso form at' with document and reader and outcome.
  a boolean called 'matched the dashed form' is outcome's "matched".
  If 'matched the dashed form' then, Return.
  'try the compact form at' with document and reader and outcome.
  a boolean called 'matched the compact form' is outcome's "matched".
  If 'matched the compact form' then, Return.
  'try a day month year at' with document and reader and outcome.
  a boolean called 'matched the day month year form' is outcome's "matched".
  If 'matched the day month year form' then, Return.
  'try a month day year at' with document and reader and outcome.

To 'the moment read from' of a text called source.
  a text called trimmed is 'the trimmed text of' of source.
  a buffer called document is "{trimmed}".
  a map called reader is {"position": 1}.
  a map called outcome is {"matched": false, "moment": 0}.
  'try an absolute moment at' with document and reader and outcome.
  a boolean called 'it matched' is outcome's "matched".
  If 'it matched' is false then, Return a number, 0.
  a number called 'the position' is reader's "position".
  If 'the position' is less than or equal to document's size then, Return a number, 0.
  Return a number, outcome's "moment".

To 'reads as a moment' of a text called source.
  a text called trimmed is 'the trimmed text of' of source.
  a buffer called document is "{trimmed}".
  a map called reader is {"position": 1}.
  a map called outcome is {"matched": false, "moment": 0}.
  'try an absolute moment at' with document and reader and outcome.
  a boolean called 'it matched' is outcome's "matched".
  If 'it matched' is false then, Return a boolean, false.
  a number called 'the position' is reader's "position".
  Return a boolean, 'the position' is greater than document's size.

(--- Relative descriptions: the half of GNU's date -d people actually
 use - an optional absolute moment, above, followed by zero or more
 relative items in either order, each applied to a running "base" moment
 held in a map so every item sees where the one before it landed. )

(A unit word, singular or plural - plural tried first, since a singular
 name is a prefix of its own plural and would otherwise steal the match.
 1 second, 2 minute, 3 hour, 4 day, 5 week, 6 month, 7 year; 0 for none.)
To 'read a unit word at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "seconds"} then, Return a number, 1.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "second"} then, Return a number, 1.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "minutes"} then, Return a number, 2.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "minute"} then, Return a number, 2.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "hours"} then, Return a number, 3.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "hour"} then, Return a number, 3.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "days"} then, Return a number, 4.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "day"} then, Return a number, 4.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "weeks"} then, Return a number, 5.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "week"} then, Return a number, 5.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "months"} then, Return a number, 6.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "month"} then, Return a number, 6.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "years"} then, Return a number, 7.
  If {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "year"} then, Return a number, 7.
  Return a number, 0.

(count of that unit, later than base - the one export each of the seven
 unit words above is spelling out.)
To 'apply a unit' with a number called base and a number called 'the unit' and a number called count.
  If 'the unit' is 1 then, Return a number, {'seconds later' of base and count}.
  If 'the unit' is 2 then, Return a number, {'minutes later' of base and count}.
  If 'the unit' is 3 then, Return a number, {'hours later' of base and count}.
  If 'the unit' is 4 then, Return a number, {'days later' of base and count}.
  If 'the unit' is 5 then, Return a number, {'weeks later' of base and count}.
  If 'the unit' is 6 then, Return a number, {'months later' of base and count}.
  Return a number, {'years later' of base and count}.

(One relative item, whatever it turns out to be, applied to state's
 "base" in place. Written into outcome's "matched"; a miss leaves both
 the reader and state untouched, so a caller can try the next thing at
 the same position - except that there is no next thing, every accepted
 word here being distinct, so a miss always means the description is
 over or malformed.)
To 'try a relative item at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called state and a map called outcome.
  a number called start is reader's "position".
  a boolean called 'it is now' is 'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "now".
  If 'it is now' then, Set outcome's "matched" to true, Return.
  a boolean called 'it is today' is 'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "today".
  If 'it is today' then, a number called base is state's "base", Set state's "base" to {'the start of the day of' of base}, Set outcome's "matched" to true, Return.
  a boolean called 'it is tomorrow' is 'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "tomorrow".
  If 'it is tomorrow' then, a number called base is state's "base", a number called 'the start of today' is {'the start of the day of' of base}, Set state's "base" to {'days later' of 'the start of today' and 1}, Set outcome's "matched" to true, Return.
  a boolean called 'it is yesterday' is 'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "yesterday".
  If 'it is yesterday' then, a number called base is state's "base", a number called 'the start of today' is {'the start of the day of' of base}, Set state's "base" to {'days later' of 'the start of today' and -1}, Set outcome's "matched" to true, Return.
  a boolean called 'says next' is 'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "next".
  a boolean called 'says last' is false.
  If 'says next' is false then, set 'says last' to {'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "last"}.
  a boolean called 'says next or last' is false.
  If 'says next' then, set 'says next or last' to true.
  If 'says last' then, set 'says next or last' to true.
  a number called 'the direction' is 1.
  If 'says last' then, set 'the direction' to -1.
  a number called 'the spaces after next or last' is 0.
  If 'says next or last' then, set 'the spaces after next or last' to {'skip spaces' with document and reader}.
  If 'says next or last' and 'the spaces after next or last' is 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the unit after next or last' is 0.
  If 'says next or last' then, set 'the unit after next or last' to {'read a unit word at' with document and reader}.
  If 'says next or last' and 'the unit after next or last' is not 0 then, a number called base is state's "base", Set state's "base" to {'apply a unit' with base and 'the unit after next or last' and 'the direction'}, Set outcome's "matched" to true, Return.
  a number called 'the weekday after next or last' is 0.
  If 'says next or last' and 'the unit after next or last' is 0 then, set 'the weekday after next or last' to {'read a weekday name at' with document and reader}.
  If 'says next or last' and 'the weekday after next or last' is 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  If 'says next' and 'the weekday after next or last' is not 0 then, a number called base is state's "base", a number called 'the day after' is {'days later' of base and 1}, Set state's "base" to {'the weekday on or after' of 'the day after' and 'the weekday after next or last'}, Set outcome's "matched" to true, Return.
  If 'says last' and 'the weekday after next or last' is not 0 then, a number called base is state's "base", a number called 'the day before' is {'days later' of base and -1}, Set state's "base" to {'the weekday on or before' of 'the day before' and 'the weekday after next or last'}, Set outcome's "matched" to true, Return.
  a number called 'the bare weekday' is 'read a weekday name at' with document and reader.
  If 'the bare weekday' is not 0 then, a number called base is state's "base", Set state's "base" to {'the weekday on or after' of base and 'the bare weekday'}, Set outcome's "matched" to true, Return.
  a number called 'the sign' is 1.
  a boolean called 'has a sign' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and "+".
  If 'has a sign' is false then, a boolean called 'has a minus' is 'the document reads' with document and reader and "-", if 'has a minus' then, set 'the sign' to -1, set 'has a sign' to true..
  If 'has a sign' then, 'skip spaces' with document and reader.
  a map called scratch is {"matched": false, "value": 0}.
  'read some digits into' with document and reader and scratch.
  a boolean called 'digits matched' is scratch's "matched".
  If 'digits matched' is false then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called count is {'the sign' multiply {scratch's "value"}}.
  a number called 'the spaces before the unit' is 'skip spaces' with document and reader.
  If 'the spaces before the unit' is 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the unit' is 'read a unit word at' with document and reader.
  If 'the unit' is 0 then, Set reader's "position" to start, Set outcome's "matched" to false, Return.
  a number called 'the position before ago' is reader's "position".
  'skip spaces' with document and reader.
  a boolean called 'has ago' is 'the document reads ignoring case' with document and reader and "ago".
  If 'has ago' is false then, Set reader's "position" to 'the position before ago'.
  If 'has ago' then, set count to {0 subtract count}.
  a number called base is state's "base".
  Set state's "base" to {'apply a unit' with base and 'the unit' and count}.
  Set outcome's "matched" to true.

(Every relative item there is, applied in turn, until one does not match
 or the text runs out; written into result's "items applied".)
To 'parse the relative items at' with a buffer called document and a map called reader and a map called state and a map called result.
  a number called 'items applied' is 0.
  a boolean called 'still going' is true.
  While 'still going',
    'skip spaces' with document and reader,
    a number called 'the position' is reader's "position",
    set 'still going' to false,
    a map called item is {"matched": false},
    if 'the position' is less than or equal to document's size then, 'try a relative item at' with document and reader and state and item.
    if item's "matched" then, increment 'items applied', set 'still going' to true..
  Set result's "items applied" to 'items applied'.

To 'the moment described by' of a text called source and a number called 'the moment it is relative to'.
  a text called trimmed is 'the trimmed text of' of source.
  a buffer called document is "{trimmed}".
  a map called reader is {"position": 1}.
  a map called outcome is {"matched": false, "moment": 0}.
  'try an absolute moment at' with document and reader and outcome.
  a boolean called 'has an absolute prefix' is outcome's "matched".
  a map called state is {"base": 0}.
  If 'has an absolute prefix' then, Set state's "base" to {outcome's "moment"}.
  If 'has an absolute prefix' is false then, Set state's "base" to 'the moment it is relative to'.
  a map called result is {"items applied": 0}.
  'parse the relative items at' with document and reader and state and result.
  a number called 'items applied' is result's "items applied".
  a boolean called 'had at least one thing' is false.
  If 'has an absolute prefix' then, set 'had at least one thing' to true.
  If 'items applied' is greater than 0 then, set 'had at least one thing' to true.
  If 'had at least one thing' is false then, Return a number, 0.
  a number called 'the final position' is reader's "position".
  If 'the final position' is less than or equal to document's size then, Return a number, 0.
  Return a number, state's "base".

To 'reads as a description' of a text called source.
  a text called trimmed is 'the trimmed text of' of source.
  a buffer called document is "{trimmed}".
  a map called reader is {"position": 1}.
  a map called outcome is {"matched": false, "moment": 0}.
  'try an absolute moment at' with document and reader and outcome.
  a boolean called 'has an absolute prefix' is outcome's "matched".
  a map called state is {"base": 0}.
  a map called result is {"items applied": 0}.
  'parse the relative items at' with document and reader and state and result.
  a number called 'items applied' is result's "items applied".
  a boolean called 'had at least one thing' is false.
  If 'has an absolute prefix' then, set 'had at least one thing' to true.
  If 'items applied' is greater than 0 then, set 'had at least one thing' to true.
  If 'had at least one thing' is false then, Return a boolean, false.
  a number called 'the final position' is reader's "position".
  Return a boolean, 'the final position' is greater than document's size.
